course: dictionary
lesson: 10839
title: Verge: the edge and the almost
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A verge is the strip of grass beside a road or path. «Councils can make wild verges, plant trees and turn lights down.» Wild verges are grassy strips left to grow, so a verge is the grass at the edge of the road.
explain: «Walk on the verge if there's no pavement» tells you that a verge can be somewhere you walk. Look at the words around it to be sure which meaning the writer means.
explain: Verge has two other meanings. «On the verge of» means very close to doing something or to something happening, as in «on the verge of tears». To verge on something means to be almost that thing, as in «verging on rude».
fact: A verge is a strip of grass beside a road or path.
fact: «On the verge of» means very close to something happening.
fact: «Verge on» means almost being something, as in «verging on rude», which means nearly rude.
fact: Verge can be a noun (a verge, verges) or a verb (to verge, verging).
fact: «Motorway verges are rarely mown» means the grass there is not often cut.
exercise: «Walk on the verge if there's no pavement.» What is a verge? | A wide road for cars | *A strip of grass beside a road or path | A bridge over a river
exercise: «She was on the verge of tears.» What does on the verge of tears mean? | *Very close to crying | Had already finished crying | Laughing loudly | Lost her way home
exercise: «The joke verged on rude.» What does verged on rude mean? | Very polite | *Almost rude | Written down | Completely silly
test: «Councils can make wild verges, plant trees and turn lights down.» What does verges mean here? | Bus stops | *Strips of grass beside roads | Tall trees | Sandy beaches
test: «Picture a kestrel over a motorway verge.» Where is the kestrel? | On a farm roof | Inside a cathedral | *Over the grass beside a motorway | In a lake
exam: Ella says «He is on the verge of tears». What does she mean? | He never cries | He is far away from tears | He has cried all day | *He is very close to crying
